From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] d3d11: a format's multisample flags follow the sample counts that work

CheckFormatSupport gave MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET, MULTISAMPLE_LOAD and MULTISAMPLE_RESOLVE only when 4 and 8 samples both worked. llvmpipe does 4 and not 8, so no format was multisample-renderable; ANGLE then reported no sample counts, Skia found no renderable format and Chromium's GPU process died at start. The flags are now given when any sample count above 1 works; CheckMultisampleQualityLevels says which.
---
diff --git a/dlls/d3d11/device.c b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
index 747fd70..dfd83b8 100644
--- a/dlls/d3d11/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
@@ -4534,12 +4534,26 @@ static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE d3d11_device_CheckFormatSupport(ID3D11Device2 *
             && (*format_support & D3D11_FORMAT_SUPPORT_BUFFER))
         *format_support |= D3D11_FORMAT_SUPPORT_SO_BUFFER;
 
-    /* d3d11 requires 4 and 8 sample counts support for formats reported to
-     * support multisample. */
+    /* Stained Glass OS (wine-sg 6097): the multisample flags say the format can be multisampled;
+     * which sample counts, CheckMultisampleQualityLevels says. They were given only when 4 and 8
+     * samples both worked -- what feature level 11 hardware must have -- so a driver that does 4
+     * and not 8 (llvmpipe: virtual machines, machines without a GPU driver) reported no
+     * multisampling at all, and ANGLE then reported no sample counts for any format: Skia found
+     * no renderable format, and Chromium's and Electron's GPU process died three times at start
+     * and fell back to software drawing. */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_MSAA_NEEDS_8
     if (wined3d_check_device_multisample_type(wined3d_adapter, params.device_type, wined3d_format,
             TRUE, WINED3D_MULTISAMPLE_4_SAMPLES, NULL) == WINED3D_OK &&
             wined3d_check_device_multisample_type(wined3d_adapter, params.device_type, wined3d_format,
             TRUE, WINED3D_MULTISAMPLE_8_SAMPLES, NULL) == WINED3D_OK)
+#else
+    if (wined3d_check_device_multisample_type(wined3d_adapter, params.device_type, wined3d_format,
+            TRUE, WINED3D_MULTISAMPLE_2_SAMPLES, NULL) == WINED3D_OK ||
+            wined3d_check_device_multisample_type(wined3d_adapter, params.device_type, wined3d_format,
+            TRUE, WINED3D_MULTISAMPLE_4_SAMPLES, NULL) == WINED3D_OK ||
+            wined3d_check_device_multisample_type(wined3d_adapter, params.device_type, wined3d_format,
+            TRUE, WINED3D_MULTISAMPLE_8_SAMPLES, NULL) == WINED3D_OK)
+#endif
     {
         *format_support |= D3D11_FORMAT_SUPPORT_MULTISAMPLE_RENDERTARGET
                 | D3D11_FORMAT_SUPPORT_MULTISAMPLE_LOAD;
